# @marcmouries/lilyjs is published privately to GitHub Packages (the lilyJS repo
# is private, and a GitHub Packages npm package inherits its repository's
# visibility). Installing it therefore requires authentication — unlike the
# public npm registry, GitHub Packages requires a token even for public packages.
#
# NO TOKEN BELONGS IN THIS FILE. It is read from the environment:
#   local dev  — export NODE_AUTH_TOKEN=<PAT with read:packages>
#   CI/deploy  — NODE_AUTH_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}, and the package
#                must grant this repository access under its "Manage Actions
#                access" settings, because a workflow's GITHUB_TOKEN is scoped
#                to its own repository and lilyJS is a different one.
#
# A missing token fails install with a 401 that does not say "set a token".
@marcmouries:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
